# Wrap-Up

In this lab, I protected the `bootcamp` PostgreSQL database using several backup and recovery techniques.

First, I created and verified a logical backup using `pg_dump` and `pg_restore`.

Second, I configured WAL archiving and created a base backup using `pg_basebackup`.

Third, I simulated a disaster by deleting records from the `students` table and used Point-in-Time Recovery to restore the database to an earlier point in time.

Finally, I created a replication user, configured PostgreSQL for streaming replication, created a standby server, and monitored the replication status and lag.

This exercise demonstrated how PostgreSQL backups, WAL archiving, Point-in-Time Recovery, and streaming replication can help protect data against accidental deletion and system failures.
